<title>UK: IBCA rates NatWest reset subordinated notes.</title>
<headline>IBCA rates NatWest reset subordinated notes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBCA, the European rating agency, said on Monday it had rated NatWest 7.75 percent reset subordinated notes AA minus.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue is limited to $500 million and the securities have no stated maturity,&quot; IBCA said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;National Westminster Bank Plc has the right to redeem the issue in whole or part on October 16, 2007, or subsequent six monthly interest payment dates,&quot; the rating agency said.</p>
<p>--International Bonds Unit +44 171 542 4041</p>
</text>
